<LearnLayout
  title="Sessions: Never Lose a Window Again — Learn — cntxt"
  description="How cntxt silently records what was open, every ~15 minutes, so nothing is ever truly lost."
  path="/learn/sessions"
>
  <a href="/learn" class="back-link">← Learn</a>
  <h1>Sessions: never lose a window again</h1>
  <p>
    In the background, every ~15 minutes, cntxt silently snapshots every
    open, cntxt-bound window — which Project or Quest it was showing, and
    its live tabs — into one history record. No manual "save a session"
    step; it just accumulates. Idling doesn't spam history: each capture is
    deduplicated against the last one.
  </p>
  <p>
    A Session survives even if the Project or Quest it was about is later
    deleted — its name is snapshotted onto the record, not looked up live.
    And unlike Trash, a Session is never auto-purged: by design, there is no
    retention or deletion of session history, ever. Restoring one reopens
    every window it recorded at once.
  </p>

